{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1474962-scion-database-app-database-development","id":1474962,"title":"Scion Database - App Database Development","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-19T04:57:44-08:00","id":1474962,"title":"Scion Database - App Database Development","content":"So, I did a thing. I'm programming in Bubble.io an app/database of cross reference for the Scion 2nd edition gods. My goal with this is to help when you are creating a character (or just for sheer curiosity) asks: &quot;Which gods have [Purview X] or [Calling Y] from any pantheon?&quot;. Then, what this thing (still in development) does, is list what you filter by the database. You can also search for direct name of the God, or list them by pantheon.<br /> <br /> The link, if I got Bubble right, is: <a href=\"https://scion-db.bubbleapps.io/version-test\" target=\"_blank\">https://scion-db.bubbleapps.io/version-test</a><br /> <br /> Feel free to visit and give some feedback. So far, some things I found out and think about developing:<br /> <br /> 1. I'm a free user of Bubble, what means many things. I can not export or import databases, so probably other people will not see or edit them for a while. What is bad since there are many other materials to add from suplements. Also, as a free user, my database is limited to 200 items. Just the gods from core books totalized 130-ish. So, I'll not add the new pantheons (or flights) for a while.<br /> <br /> 2. Implement an actual cross reference is a must and I'll work on it probably today. The system works fine for filtering one of the items of the scroll down lists, but make it cross will probably be a little more complex (&quot;Which Gods are Tricksters from Sh\u00e9n?&quot; for instance). Just an aesthetics idea, but maybe add colored backgrounds to search results would be nice (ie: gray for Aesir, red for \u00d2rish\u00e1, 